---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { about } from "../content";
import PageHero from "@dst/ui/PageHero.astro";
---
<Layout
  prose title={about.title} description={about.description}>
  <PageHero
    title={about.h1}
    image="/covers/about.jpg"
    imageAlt="A glowing magenta film strip curving diagonally across a near-black ground"
    imageKind="generated"
  >
    <p class="lede">{about.lede}</p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p set:html={`<strong>aivideo.zone</strong> follows AI video from both ends: the generative models that make the footage — Kling, Grok Imagine, LTX, MiniMax and the rest — and the tools it is then cut, extended and repaired in, ComfyUI first among them. News when something ships or shuts down, guides when a change needs more than a paragraph, and for screenwriters, how each model wants a scene written.`} />
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>The rules</h2>
    <ol class="rules">
      <li>
        <h3>Every fact names where it came from, and when we last looked</h3>
        <p>The maker's release notes, model card or documentation first, and a report only where the maker has said nothing. The source and the date it was checked are printed on the entry.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Specifications are the maker's, and are called that</h3>
        <p>A resolution, a clip length or a parameter count is what the maker published. Where we have not run a model ourselves, the page says what was announced, not what it does on your machine.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Prices are dated</h3>
        <p>AI video is billed by the second and the price moves. A price on this site is the one on the maker's own page on the day the entry says we checked it.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Nothing here is paid for</h3>
        <p>No tool or model pays to be covered, ranked or linked. Links to makers' sites go out through a redirect that passes them nothing.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>A page exists when there is something to put on it</h3>
        <p>A tool gets a page of its own once there are two stories about it, and not before.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .rules {
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: rule;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .rules li {
    counter-increment: rule;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr;
    gap: 0 var(--space-2);
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .rules li::before {
    content: counter(rule);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .rules h3 { margin: 0; font-size: var(--step-0); }
  .rules p { margin: 0.25em 0 0; grid-column: 2; max-width: 62ch; color: var(--ink-muted); }
</style>
